# GitHub issue #27

**Repository:** alexisNorthcoders/snake-colyseus
**URL:** https://github.com/alexisNorthcoders/snake-colyseus/issues/27
**State:** OPEN
**Labels:** ready-for-agent
**Title:** Room game speed

## Body
## What to build

Each room runs at its own speed, measured in ticks (moves) per second and chosen when the room is created: `create`/`joinOrCreate("snake", { speed: n })`. Every client can read the speed from room state. Today it's fixed at 8 ticks per second (`gameConfig.fps`). With this, the speed can be tuned without redeploying.

**Decisions:**

- `speed` is an integer number of ticks per second, clamped to 4–15. A missing or invalid value falls back to the default, which stays 8 until playtesting says otherwise.
- The value is fixed when the room is created. The simulation interval is `1000 / speed`.
- The speed is synced to clients in `GameState` as the tick length in ms, so the client can pace its animation to match.
- Matchmaking filters on `speed`, so a `joinOrCreate` never puts a player into a room running at a different speed. Production clients all send the default, so production matchmaking is unchanged.
- Countdown timing is unaffected.
- `botReactionTicks` (#26) stays counted in ticks, so its real-time delay scales with speed. That's fine: slower games give the bot slower reflexes as well.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] A room created with `speed` runs its simulation at that many ticks per second; invalid values fall back to 8, and it's clamped to 4–15
- [ ] The tick length is synced in room state and is correct for the room's speed
- [ ] `joinOrCreate` with different speeds lands in different rooms, and with the same speed lands in the same room
- [ ] With no `speed`, behaviour is identical to today (existing tests pass)

## Blocked by

None - can start immediately

